Subject: [PATCH] feat: Win-Back manual enrollment UI, brand voice and page
 audit standalone triggers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes the two remaining Showtime UI gaps confirmed by scanning the actual
dashboard structure (not assumed): Win-Back had no way to manually enroll
a new prospect anywhere (the pipeline toolbar had search+refresh only, the
API route was GET-only, and the generic WorkersPanel Run button explicitly
refuses win-back/pile-on since they're webhook-only) — same shape gap as
Pile-On before that fix. Brand voice extraction and confirmation page
audit had ZERO UI trigger anywhere, gated or not — chat was the only way
to run either at all.

Win-Back: same preview-then-confirm two-step modal as Pile-On's, added to
win-back-pipeline.tsx's toolbar, backed by a new
previewManualWinBackEnrollment (chat-winback.ts) that mirrors
enrollProspectInWinBack's own validation chain read-only. Deliberately NO
force override, unlike Pile-On — an existing active enrollment for the
same prospect is a genuine "already in this cadence" state, not a soft
duplicate signal, so enrolling again would mean two live cadences
messaging the same person.

Brand voice / page audit: a shared RunPinDownPieceButton (domain or URL
input + trigger) added directly into DeliverablesPanel — brand voice's
existing fallback-state row, and a new empty-state row for page audit
(previously the whole row didn't render until one existed). Both post to
a new /api/engagements/[id]/pin-down/run-piece route that calls the exact
same triggerVoiceExtractionForEngagement / triggerPageAuditForEngagement
functions Teammates chat already uses — zero new business logic, just a
second way to reach code already shipped and verified this session.

